    <statement><p>Represent the function <m>\displaystyle \frac{3}{(1 - 6 x)}</m> as a power series 
<m>\displaystyle f(x) = \sum_{n=0}^\infty c_n x^n</m></p>
<p><m>c_0 =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>c_1 =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><m>c_2 =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><m>c_3 =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p><m>c_4 =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>Find the radius of convergence <m>R =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0006"/>  .</p>
